      "content": "exactly. it's like they're being careful to stay under the radar of official HR policies so they can claim it's just \"operational noise\" if i bring it up. i've noticed they've even started CC'ing my manager on things that used to be private, which feels like they're building a paper trail against me too. if i want to show a lawyer that this is a coordinated campaign to force a breakdown, should i start looking for connections between the people making these \"errors\" and the ones who handle my severance package? like, is there a way to map out if the same group of people is involved in all these little disruptions?",
